  "id": "active-attention",
  "term": "active attention",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, active attention is the mind’s effort to keep certain ideas before it by selecting, emphasizing, and holding them a little longer. Rather than producing thoughts from nothing, it guides what comes next in thinking and action by favoring some ideas over others.",
